### Reject out-of-range recording scale values

**Severity:** `medium`

`ZoomItSettingsFunctionData.SetState` forwards the DSC `RecordScaling` value directly to the native interop. Unlike the Settings UI, this path does not constrain the value to 10–100 before writing it; the native code stores it unchanged, and recording uses it to scale frame dimensions. Reject values outside the supported range before `SaveSettingsJson`, and add boundary tests for the DSC setter.

```suggestion
        var recordScaling = _output.Settings?.Properties?.RecordScaling;
        if (recordScaling?.Value is < 10 or > 100)
        {
            throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException(nameof(ZoomItProperties.RecordScaling), "RecordScaling must be between 10 and 100.");
        }

        SaveSettingsJson(JsonSerializer.Serialize(_output.Settings, _serializerOptions));
```
